            {
              "text": "Brisbane’s prestige property landscape is characterized by a strong alignment between custom subtropical architecture (such as works by Shaun Lockyer, Joe Adsett, and Graya) and digital-first, cinematic marketing. \n\nAgencies and boutique specialist teams in Brisbane with the strongest reputations for **modern social media marketing, high-impact video campaigns, and architectural homes** include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. WHITEFOX Real Estate (Brisbane)\n* **The Vibe:** Bold, editorial, cinematic, and digitally native.\n* **Why They Fit:** Originally founded in Melbourne and known for disrupting real estate marketing across Australia, WHITEFOX expanded into Brisbane (based on James Street in Fortitude Valley). Their entire model revolves around **high-production video, razor-sharp Instagram/TikTok content, and ditching traditional advertising templates**.\n* **Video & Social Style:** They produce distinct, stylized property films and fast-paced episodic social videos (such as their signature *\"THE DEAL\"* segments). Their production uses cinema-grade cameras, curated music, and lifestyle framing rather than static walk-throughs.\n* **Architectural Alignment:** Highly aligned with contemporary luxury builds, cutting-edge developer projects, and trophy modern homes—including builds by leading Queensland developer-builders like Graya.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Heath Williams (Place New Farm)\n* **The Vibe:** Architectural authority, design-literate storytelling, and refined editorial elegance.\n* **Why They Fit:** While Place is a larger independent network, Heath Williams operates a dedicated boutique prestige unit that is widely recognized as **Brisbane’s benchmark for architectural real estate**. With a background in interior architecture, Williams markets homes through the lens of design pedigree rather than generic sales tropes.\n* **Video & Social Style:** Instead of fast-paced gimmicks, the team produces **mini-documentaries and immersive architectural films**. These videos detail materiality, natural light, spatial geometry, and the architect’s intent (often featuring the architects themselves). He regularly collaborates with premier design platforms like *The Local Project* and maintains a highly curated architectural Instagram aesthetic.\n* **Architectural Alignment:** The go-to representative for Brisbane’s most celebrated design studios, including Shaun Lockyer Architects, Paul Owen, and DM2 Architecture.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Adcock Prestige\n* **The Vibe:** High-end independent prestige, riverfront authority, and lifestyle video production.\n* **Why They Fit:** Founded by Jason Adcock, Adcock Prestige is a true boutique agency dedicated exclusively to the upper end of Brisbane’s market (inner-west, riverfront, and prestige enclaves). \n* **Video & Social Style:** Adcock was an early adopter of **host-led cinematic video walk-throughs** and heavy social media ad-targeting. Their campaigns feature sweeping drone sequences, twilight visual storytelling, and regular market-update videos across YouTube, Facebook, and Instagram that attract both interstate and international expat buyers.\n* **Architectural Alignment:** Sells many of Brisbane’s landmark riverfront architectural estates, brutalist concrete builds, and Frank Lloyd Wright-inspired modernist residences in suburbs like Indooroopilly, St Lucia, and Hamilton.\n\n---\n\n### 4. NGU Real Estate\n* **The Vibe:** Viral, theatrical, disruptive, and unapologetically high-impact.\n* **Why They Fit:** Founded by Emil Juresic, NGU (\"Never Give Up\") pioneered the **viral, blockbuster-style property video** trend in Queensland. If you are looking for video content designed to generate hundreds of thousands of organic views and mainstream media pickup, NGU is the most visible player.\n* **Video & Social Style:** Their campaigns resemble mini-movies featuring cinematic storylines, supercars, luxury fashion models, lifestyle narratives, and energetic drone choreography. Their social media distribution generates immense buzz, appealing directly to high-net-worth buyers who respond to visible luxury and status.\n* **Architectural Alignment:** Contemporary mega-mansions, bold modern concrete estates, and sprawling resort-style residences.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Ray White New Farm (Prestige Team / Matt Lancashire)\n* **The Vibe:** High-volume prestige powerhouses with bespoke boutique production.\n* **Why They Fit:** Although operating under the Ray White franchise banner, Ray White New Farm functions largely as an autonomous prestige powerhouse dominating Brisbane's peninsula suburbs (Teneriffe, New Farm, Hamilton Hill). \n* **Video & Social Style:** Matt Lancashire and his prestige team invest heavily in **bespoke lifestyle video campaigns and active Instagram reels/stories**. They frequently tease off-market architectural builds in production and leverage first-look social tours before properties even hit portals.\n* **Architectural Alignment:** Routinely represents Brisbane’s highest-profile architectural record-breakers, partnering frequently with premier residential architects and high-end luxury builders.\n\n---\n\n### Which Should You Look At?\n* **For architectural purism & design storytelling:** Heath Williams (Place New Farm).\n* **For sleek, modern, editorial-style social marketing:** WHITEFOX Real Estate.\n* **For maximum viral buzz, high-production drama, and reach:** NGU Real Estate.\n* **For established luxury, riverfront estates, and polished walkthroughs:** Adcock Prestige.",
